WEBVTT

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:08.190
Watching high-level games and 
playing high-level opponents...

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.750
Both are important.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:18.120
But even more important is training hard 
with high-level players on your own team.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:22.080
There is nothing more effective
for improving your own skills.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.600
Make sure you're teaching each other. Got it?

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.100
Yes, sir!

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:17.720
I'm the coach of Keijo's rugby team,
Haijima Yuji.

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:21.240
Thank you for agreeing 
to this joint practice session.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.770
<b>Episode 12
Joint Practice</b>

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.470
I'm Komori.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:28.980
We actually watched a video of your game
against Sagami from the other day.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:36.140
Sagami's beaten us several times, but you 
were their equals in the second half.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:37.760
It was a humdinger of a game.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:41.720
I heard that Jinko had a new coach,

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:46.410
and I was hoping my boys
could learn from you...

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.770
I couldn't have hoped for more.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.640
Thank you for inviting us.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.540
Sumiaki! Sumiaki!

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.190
He used to coach the national team?

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.060
What should I do? I really 
want his autograph!

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.650
Ow! Miyuki-kun, that hurts!

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.240
<b>Squeeze
Squeeze
Squeeze</b>

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.240
Your hands are digging into me!

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.240
He's so cool!

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.200
Sekizan, I watched your game against Sagami!

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.900
It was amazing!

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:05.310
But I was worried for you!

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:06.730
You guys gave it everything.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.250
You were cool, though!

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.120
Yeah. By the way, could you 
do something about them?

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.480
It's Oharano-kun!

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.630
<b>Ugh, 
I really 
want to 
go home...</b>

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.630
Hello!

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.400
Hey, idiots! How long are you 
gonna keep flappin' your gums?

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.350
Shake a leg and get warmed up, you morons!

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.560
Sorry. My team is full of boisterous boys.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.360
I was about to say the same thing.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.230
I have a feeling we'll get along, you and I.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:44.130
Since we have so many players,
why don't we split into forwards and backs?

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.740
Good idea.

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:48.580
Huh? Gion-kun?

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.690
The backs are over there.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:52.440
I'm staying with the forwards.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:53.100
What?

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.580
Starting today,

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.710
I'm a flanker!

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.340
What?

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:04.100
Hey, the little guy's found his voice!

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.280
Welcome to the forwards!

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.620
Gion... a flanker?

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:08.720
Seriously?

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.180
Welcome, welcome!

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.980
Welcome to the world of the forwards!

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.980
What? Sumiaki and Kenji are both over there?

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.660
This is the first I'm hearing about it.

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:15.200
Let's be friends, short stuff!

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:16.080
Well, you see, Kanagawa's number one...

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:20.610
Uh, I mean, number two flanker 
told me I'd make a good one.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:21.990
Starting today, we're going to be 
practicing <i>real</i> hard together!

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:24.240
What? You mean the Kirishima 
brothers who play for Ryoin?

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.510
You got that? We're <i>real</i> tough!

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:25.010
Prepare yourself!

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:28.690
Either way, we don't have enough 
forwards coming through the ranks.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:31.500
Why don't we see how it goes?

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:36.120
Since it's a joint practice session, 
let's form a scrum.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.180
Okay.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:39.170
I want to be in a scrum!

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.690
Scrums are super cool...

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.340
I want to learn how to do them, too.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.530
You've got good taste.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:51.600
All right, then. You can 
join our scrum as a flanker.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.680
All right!

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.770
Sorry. Thanks for this.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:58.530
A scrum is made up of three rows of forwards.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:01.530
#1 to #3 are the front row.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.030
#4 and #5 are the second row.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.550
#6 to #8 are the back row.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:07.570
Gotcha.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.380
Have you ever done the turtle?

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:11.450
Yeah, I'm great at it.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.460
That's the basic posture.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:15.670
Try to push my backside with your shoulder.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.120
O-Okay.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:23.090
I'm the world's best hooker, Taira Tadakazu!

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.090
Okay, let's get started.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.240
Whoa...

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:33.020
Some flankers just pretend to push 
since they're on the outside edge.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:36.800
But you don't get any 
easy rides in a Keijo scrum.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:39.520
Push as hard as you can.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:43.860
Crouch, bind, set!

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.200
You're not pushing hard enough!

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.050
Get lower! Straighten your back!

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:55.700
You can dig deeper than that!

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:01.900
Okay.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.470
That was terrible.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.670
Well, it <i>was </i>your first time.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.270
You must've felt it during 
the Sagami game, too.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:16.960
When an entire team gives 
everything they've got.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:20.730
That combined effort becomes 
the true strength of the team.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:23.070
And it's not just during games...

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:25.730
Give it your all in practice sessions, too.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:31.740
Dammit. I want to push, too...

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:37.370
More! Let me be in more scrums!

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:45.930
The facial expressions of the Keijo kids
during practice are admirable.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:49.380
Thank you. I feel the same way
about your charges.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.810
Jinko's facial expressions 
are completely different

00:06:51.810 --> 00:06:54.390
from a month ago when we played each other.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.660
What on earth have you taught them?

00:06:57.660 --> 00:07:02.080
What I can tell you is that we didn't
cover facial expressions in our sessions.

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:06.000
Have you decided now?

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:09.450
Okay, get some water!

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.760
In 15 minutes, we'll play a game!

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:17.020
Split into Teams A and B.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.040
Come get your bibs.

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:24.160
Since we're both wearing this color, 
I should escape injury this time.

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:26.520
Don't be mean.

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:27.550
Sorry.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.300
Wow, that's a crazy lineup.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.800
Don't hold back just because 
it's a practice game!

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:39.730
It still matters who wins and loses. You hear?

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:44.530
They're lucky they get to play 
on the same team as Keijo.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:48.320
I bet they'll learn a few things. 
Looks like it'll be fun.

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:50.520
Team B will kick off.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:51.410
Begin!

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:58.740
Sekizan!

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:10.380
Dammit. They're already going all out.

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:35.700
What?

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.320
An interception!

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:38.780
Crap! Get back there!

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:42.660
Miyuki-kun, their #8...

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:47.170
...always throws an offload 
pass when he's tackled.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:50.330
<i>I watched the video of
the Jinko vs. Sagami game.</i>

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:52.340
<i>He was right.</i>

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:59.430
<i>He waits until he's tackled to pass,
which is known as an "offload pass."</i>

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:02.340
<i>Since Sekizan-senpai's so strong,</i>

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.940
<i>he can keep the ball in play
even after he's tackled.</i>

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:08.170
<i>Because of that, it's become a habit.</i>

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:11.190
<i>He probably hasn't even noticed it himself.</i>

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:14.130
<i>Neither have the other Jinko players.</i>

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.450
You're not going anywhere!

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:21.680
<i>He's probably not even
giving it a second thought.</i>

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:25.210
Please...

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:39.730
That was fast. Their #10 sure is good.

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:41.850
Well, yeah, the #10 is good,

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:45.600
but doesn't Iwashimizu's play 
seem different from usual?

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:51.290
<i>That feeling brings back memories.</i>

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:57.920
<i>That's right. Iwashimizu is the type of guy
who can keep up with better players.</i>

00:10:00.140 --> 00:10:03.460
<i>There's a terrifying duo on this team.</i>

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.020
<b>I can't believe
 we're in another 
episode</b>

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.020
<b>Let's 
pull, 
pull, 
pull!!</b>

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:09.020
<b>Please stop...</b>

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:11.040
<b>Oh, it's not that 
bad once you 
get used to it</b>

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.000
<b>I can't believe 
you do everything 
yourself, Umenon</b>

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.000
<b>I admire you~
I could never do that...</b>

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.000
<b>What?</b>

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:12.000
<b>Yeah...</b>

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:16.470
Matsu-san, aren't you happy?

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:20.040
We didn't get to play in
the last game against Keijo.

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:24.400
This may only be practice, 
but a game's a game.

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:27.510
Now we can tackle all the guys
we wanted to tackle!

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:29.060
Ya-ha!

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.630
Ebumi-senpai's scary...

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:34.570
You should try to keep 
the ball away from him.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:35.440
Sure.

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:42.060
Well, he's up against Yoichi, 
Keijo's fastest runner, on that wing.

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:43.460
You still think he's dangerous?

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:46.210
Maybe.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.000
Understood.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:50.870
Centers, you got a second?

00:10:55.540 --> 00:11:00.990
Interesting. I see a few boys 
making some unusual moves.

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:05.370
High school students haven't 
settled on their own styles yet.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:08.890
They're easily influenced.

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:13.360
You're right. It really is interesting.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:21.410
It's Team A's ball!

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.040
They're going to move
the ball to the outside!

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:27.160
Give me the ball!

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:31.540
Bastard!

00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:39.130
<i>I wanted to use Ebumi to alter 
the flow of the game, but...</i>

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.260
Come on! Give me the ball!

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:45.600
<i>...they know what we're up to.</i>

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:52.390
<i>Jinko's fly-half isn't Etsugo...</i>

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:57.230
<i>He's not particularly 
fast or good at passing.</i>

00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:59.760
<i>He's big, but...</i>

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:02.860
<i>I can knock him down.</i>

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:10.790
<i>I guess this is my only option.</i>

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.160
Wow, something's coming my way.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:20.130
It's got some distance on it!

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.220
Yoichi, run!

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:36.690
It landed in the in-goal area!

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.190
What?

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.890
You're slow.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:59.290
Ogi, how could you let him beat you?!

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:03.420
No way! I never thought I'd lose
in a battle of speed!

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:07.930
Sorry, Miyukichi! Don't be mad!

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:19.440
<i>Yikes. I can't go straight to kicking 
and relying on Ebumi's legs all the time.</i>

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:22.070
This game's starting to come to the boil.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.690
Good. I'm all fired up now.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.600
That's one try each.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:31.830
It's kinda amazing.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:34.160
Get the ball and
 run super fast

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:34.160
Throw the ball 
before you fall down

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:34.160
<b>Kick super far when 
everything goes scrappy</b>

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:41.500
We're making a substitution.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.970
These three are in.

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:49.800
Noka's subbing in for Suwa as Team A's #14.

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:53.080
Ohie's subbing in for Shinshi at #1.

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:57.040
Gion's subbing in for Masa as #7.

00:13:58.180 --> 00:14:00.070
All right!

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:02.700
Yeah!

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:02.690
Good for you, Gion.

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:07.230
That boy sure is full of beans.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:13.070
I'm sorry for making you
 play him as a flanker.

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:17.640
Don't be. The more passionate a boy is, 
the more I want him to learn.

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:23.910
I can't wait to see how someone 
who's serious about taking notes plays.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.940
You're already playing flanker, huh?

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:28.240
Thanks for accommodating me.

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:30.340
That's the spirit.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:37.640
Kenji!

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:45.150
Play will resume. Team B to kick off.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:49.620
Gion, are you up to speed 
on your positioning?

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:50.710
I got it.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:57.640
Team A's making a lot of mistakes.

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:01.020
Though, I guess, being a mixed team,
they can't help that.

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:02.330
You're right.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:06.170
Team B seems to be moving
the ball around well, though.

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.380
Move up, winger!

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:13.210
Your fly-half's doing a good job.

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:16.140
You mean, Miyuki? He's a first-year.

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:18.020
Is that so?

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:21.250
What a terrifying first-year.

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:27.030
He closely monitors the field
and every player on it.

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:28.490
Yukissan!

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:36.390
<i>One of the subs...
He looks wet behind the ears.</i>

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:38.660
<i>I can just sidestep him.</i>

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:41.670
What?!

00:15:56.010 --> 00:16:01.510
Huh? That kid's out of control,
but he moves well.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:16.340
<i>Kenji's energy is amazing,
but he's not where a flanker should be.</i>

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:18.580
<i>He only has eyes for the ball.</i>

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:20.680
<i>But...</i>

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:25.540
Gion, are you sure you 
know how to play flanker?

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:28.340
I know.

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.530
What does a flanker do?

00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:34.300
Everything.

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:38.550
Whether it's attacking or defending, 
they're the first ones on the scene.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:42.810
<i>I'm still no good at handling the ball.</i>

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:47.720
They arrive at the ball 
quicker than everyone else.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.030
<i>But I can at least do that!</i>

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:56.410
<i>You're everywhere, Kenji!</i>

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:02.000
But energy alone isn't
 enough to stop me, Kenji!

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:10.340
<i>What's he looking at?</i>

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:15.360
Get the ball out! Quick!

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:19.100
Dammit...

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:21.670
Getting the ball back is hard.

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:24.850
Oh, it's you.

00:17:28.220 --> 00:17:31.810
<i>Where was he looking when he tackled me?</i>

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:37.360
<i>Where?</i>

00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:44.550
<i>Their bellybuttons!</i>

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:48.670
<i>He's only looking at their torsos.</i>

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:57.590
<i>You can move your feet or feint with your 
upper body, but you can't move your torso.</i>

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:01.100
<i>That's what he's been aiming at!</i>

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:04.350
Kenji, you've gotten better!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:05.850
Yeah.

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:10.360
Their bellies are the biggest targets
and the easiest to tackle.

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:14.860
And when I aim for their legs, 
it hurts when they kick me.

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:16.640
Again!

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:21.850
His movements are pretty good.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.870
Though, it seems like he's playing
without using his brain...

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:28.460
Pass!

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:32.830
That pass...

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:34.840
This time!

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:43.910
Team B, forward throw.

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:45.560
That's enough.

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:47.350
What?

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.810
Ow.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.330
What?

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:53.310
Game's over. Gather round!

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:55.990
What? It's over?

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:57.500
That was weak.

00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:58.570
Ebumi!

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:01.220
Oh, right. It's just practice.

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:02.330
That was a good workout.

00:19:01.220 --> 00:19:04.830
I wish we could play for 60 minutes.

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:04.830
Yeah, let's do it.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:07.820
No! Just a little longer!

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:11.300
Shut up, Miyuki.
We don't have the time, idiot.

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:13.840
Then, let's play again tomorrow!

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:18.590
Both teams showed some good moves.

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:23.210
You probably learned a lot
from each other, too.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:27.820
You did well. It was a good fight.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.420
Good work, guys.

00:19:32.420 --> 00:19:35.570
We're making rice balls, so help yourselves.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:38.530
Rice balls again? What's in them?

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.370
You have a choice of plums or seaweed.

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:42.070
If you don't like it, don't eat it.

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:45.040
Rice balls!

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:48.580
See? Jinko's not complaining.

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:51.580
Riechin, you're so dexterous.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.100
I can't make mine triangular.

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:56.710
It's because I always make them for the boys.

00:19:56.710 --> 00:20:00.570
You wouldn't be able to make enough for
your team by yourself, would you, Umenon?

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:03.020
Which ones are Riechin's rice balls?

00:20:03.020 --> 00:20:05.850
I want the ones made by 
the girl with the short hair.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:08.980
Kenji...

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:11.090
I wanted to play more!

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:14.300
Shut it, you! I'm hungry.

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:17.300
Sumiaki!

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:19.370
Miyuki-kun, aren't you going to eat?

00:20:19.810 --> 00:20:21.780
I will...

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:25.110
Has he always been like this?

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:27.570
Yeah, he hasn't changed.

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:31.660
By the way, Miyuki-kun...

00:20:32.700 --> 00:20:36.240
Do you remember Sagami's Hanadate-kun?

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:37.830
Hanadate...

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:41.670
Oh, that guy who tried to provoke you
during your last game?

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:43.680
Y-Yeah...

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:47.600
Yeah. If I remember correctly...

00:20:48.130 --> 00:20:52.850
When we played against Asakura 
Middle School in the semi-finals...

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:55.850
he was sat on the bench the whole time.

00:20:56.610 --> 00:21:02.050
I think he was the guy who treated 
everyone who played to an evil glare.

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:06.580
What did he say to you?

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:11.590
Don't you think it's mean 
to call someone bad?

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:14.250
You got wound up over that?

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:15.650
Iwashimizu.

00:21:18.010 --> 00:21:18.750
Y-Yes, sir.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:25.220
So you can play like that, huh?

00:21:26.270 --> 00:21:28.070
That was a frustrating experience.

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:36.100
Captain!

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:37.980
How'd I do today?

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:41.300
I moved around a lot
and tackled a lot of guys!

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:43.530
<b>Praise me</b>

00:21:41.300 --> 00:21:42.800
Wasn't I amazing?

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:43.530
<b>Come on, 
praise me</b>

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:55.040
<b>Squeeze</b>

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:48.480
You didn't even touch the ball!

00:21:48.480 --> 00:21:50.450
You just ran around the field!

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:52.420
And stop hitting everyone in the midriff!

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:54.300
What happened to tackling their feet?!

00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:55.720
You've got a lot to learn!

00:21:55.720 --> 00:21:57.530
Sekizan, you're taking it too far!

00:21:56.650 --> 00:21:59.150
What are we going to do, Coach?

00:21:57.530 --> 00:21:59.150
There's a lot to playing flanker.

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:00.380
We're going to hold a review meeting.

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:00.960
Good question.

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:01.540
What?

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:05.950
We may have taught our opponents <i>too</i> much...

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:12.800
Things are about to get interesting.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
<b>Next Time: "Let's Go To Ryogoku Together"</b>

00:23:46.080 --> 00:23:49.170
Next time: "Let's Go To Ryogoku Together."
